    "result_text": "The acceptance suite is the entire test set. Everything is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity. All 60 checkpoint test classes (70 tests) pass with 0 failures.\n\n### What changed\n\n**1. Version-2 region code inside the identifiers** \u2014 `Owner.java`\n- Added a fixed `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` and a new `identityRegionCode()` method that returns the plain region prefixed with the tag (e.g. `\"V2NSW\"`).\n- `getIdentityKey()` now mixes `identityRegionCode()` into the SHA-256 input, so the key changes but stays 64 lowercase hex.\n- Crucially, `getLocality()`, `getTimezone()` and `getOwnerSegment()` are untouched, so the user-facing `locality` stays the plain region (`\"NSW\"`) and the segment's area derivation stays plain.\n\n**2. memberId and householdId rederived** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`\n- `memberIdBase()` uses `identityRegionCode()` as the region prefix (member ids now look like `V2NSW27\u2026`).\n- `householdId(owner)` now folds `identityRegionCode()` into its hash input. Because the region derives from the same postcode/city that already defines a household, owners sharing a last name + postcode still resolve to the same household id.\n\n**3. Audit event \u2192 schema version 2**\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` gained a leading `schemaVersion` field, emitted as `2`; the primary identifier is the v2 memberId.\n\n**4. Response shape** \u2014 `openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper.java`\n- Added an `OwnerIdentity` schema and grouped `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId` under a nested `identity` object; removed them from the top level.\n- Added a top-level integer `apiVersion` of `2`.\n- The MapStruct mapper populates `identity.*` from the owner and sets `apiVersion` to 2.\n\nRequest fields (`OwnerFields`) were left unchanged, as required.\n\nEvery identifier now differs from its version-1 form (no v1 value is reproduced), while `locality`, `timezone` and the owner segment remain the plain region.",
